ny animosity between Sony and Disney is  now put aside and the two companies are  working very very well with each other  and an example of this is the Morbius  trailer there were some big connections  to the Marvel Cinematic Universe  spider-man in the Morbius trailer of  course we have the connection to  spider-man far from home where we saw  the picture of spider-man on the wall  and over it it said murderer which is  obviously referring to the post-credits  scene of spider-man far from home where  Mysterio revealed spider-man's identity  as Peter Parker and he also framed him  as  a murderer and then of course we have  Michael Keaton's character vulture  appearing and talking to Morbius as well  who of course was in spider-man  homecoming so right now the studios are  playing well with each other and  currently there are no plans to have  spider-man exit the MCU at any point in  time even after the next two spider-man  films the two studios are playing so  well with each other that he says that  he has indeed heard that the studios are  still planning a spider-man spin-off  series for Disney Plus and that he hears  that it's still looking to be spider-man  2099 and we've actually had more proof  that the studio's are playing well with  each other  Gina price bifid who has recently signed  on to direct Sony silver and black film  which was going to star silver sable and  black cat recently told us in an  interview with The Hollywood Reporter  that Disney Plus was an option for them  now the project has been scrapped so  don't expect a movie or a Disney Plus  show but the main point to take away  from this is this was a property that  was very similar to spider-man it was a  Marvel sony project that was supposed to  exist within Sony's spider-verse but  Marvel Studios and Disney said that they  could make a Disney Plus show out of it  this is another sign that the studios  are playing incredibly well with each  other right now both realize that  spider-man is a bi